 Queueker: Project Report

 1. Abstract

Queueker is an innovative, real-time, domain-specific queue management system designed to streamline customer flow and optimize administrative control. The system provides independent login portals for various institutions (such as healthcare clinics, banks, or educational administrative offices), ensuring domain isolation and security. By leveraging modern real-time WebSockets, Queueker allows customers to remotely and virtually join queues while empowering administrators to efficiently manage queue processing, reducing physical waiting times and enhancing overall operational efficiency.

2. Problem Statement

Managing physical queues across multiple institutional domains often leads to chaotic operational environments, customer dissatisfaction due to prolonged waiting times, and inefficiencies in service deployment. Traditional solutions lack real-time updates and are often rigidly structured as single-domain applications, making it difficult to host varying types of institutions (e.g., healthcare vs retail) securely on a unified platform. There is a pressing need for a system that isolated queues based on domain authentication, updates token progression in real-time, and guarantees an intuitive customer & administrator experience without cross-contamination of sensitive data.

